==English==
[[File:Shallots-Whole.jpg|right|thumb|Shallots (bulbs of ''Allium ascalonium'')]]

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|fr|échalote}}, from {{der|en|frm|eschalote}}, alteration of {{der|en|fro|eschaloigne}}, from {{der|en|ML.|escalonia}}, from {{der|en|la|ascalonia|ascalonia (cēpa)|gloss=onion of [[Ashkelon]]}}. {{doublet|en|scallion}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈʃælət/|/ʃəˈlɑt/|a=GA}}
* {{IPA|en|/ʃəˈlɒt/|a=RP}}
* {{rhymes|en|ælət|ɒt|s=2}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-shallot.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# Any vegetable of certain species in the [[onion]] family.
## ''[[Allium ascalonium]]''.
## {{taxfmt|Allium oschaninii|species}}.
# Any small onion.
# {{lb|en|New Orleans|Australia}} A [[scallion]].

